iliary Tract Disease: bile duct disease, bile reflux, biliary tract neoplasm (disease)\n\nRelated to Vascular Liver Disease (e.g., Budd-Chiari syndrome, other hepatic vein occlusions): aagenaes syndrome, abdominal and pelvic region disorder, autosomal dominant polycystic liver disease\n\nRelated to Acute Pancreatitis with Complications: pancreas disease\n\n[Indirect reasoning chains (PrimeKG 2-hop):]\n  A 23-year-old woman presents to the emergency department with severe abdominal pain → abdominal distention → Acute Cholangitis / Biliary Tract Disease\n  A 23-year-old woman presents to the emergency department with severe abdominal pain → arthralgia → Acute Cholangitis / Biliary Tract Disease\n  A 23-year-old woman presents to the emergency department with severe abdominal pain → abdominal distention → Vascular Liver Disease (e.g., Budd-Chiari syndrome, other hepatic vein occlusions)"}
